edical data which the United  States government was rumored to have  used for their own purposes during the  Korean War so we don't really we won't  know the truth about this until the  records are released  however these records are actually in  the process of being systematically  destroyed as writers unearth them I mean  this has been enough of a concern to  make certain politicians like senator  Feinstein  protest against the thesis destruction  so it's just I think it's important for  us to know that keep you know even 50  years after the fact there are forces  that political forces that are trying to  suppress this history I'd also I'd like  to to add that it is lobby groups such  as the Global Alliance that have forced  change in other places in France for  example it was a lobby group of  civilians of the the children and  grandchildren of victims that forced  change in that country as well and as as  I mentioned there there have been trials  in France there's been a complete not a  complete turnaround there's still a  great deal of discussion about the truth  of post-war French history but  tremendous efforts are being made and it  came about as a result of lobbying  other people well many people know the  movie yeah  bridge over the river kwai won the Oscar  in 1956 but nobody really know which  Japanese company were behind the  enslavement and turned out to be  headquartered in Chicago Mitsubishi  there are as many as a 10 million people  enslaved and more than half then died 37  percent American POWs I Indians wavered  and today the US government is the one  blocking justice and the Japanese are  coming to San Francisco in September to  mark the fifth anniversary of the peace  treaty yet  the same time and refused to apologize  would you comment on your attitude well  all I can say is that I'm sure your  group will be there to meet them yes you  mentioned during the course year talk  the influence of the internet on many of  these events now and in the c